findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. TEA wrote
    config loading tests but none that distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors. Reviewer did not mention this issue.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-209 tests and reviewer marked 'VERIFIED: CliError::Display\
    \ does not leak tokens or internal details'. However the Io(#[error(transparent)])\
    \ vector that forwards full OS error details to stderr was missed \u2014 reviewer's\
    \ verification was incorrect, and TEA's CWE-209 tests passed despite the leak\
    \ existing."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote 'header injection (CRLF/null bytes)' tests in cli_security.rs
    and cli_siem_client.rs. Dev implemented validate_header_value() with CRLF rejection.
    Reviewer noted 'Cli.tenant is Option<String> not Option<TenantId>' but accepted
    it. The injection vector is defended but the type-safe TenantId approach was not
    adopted.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #9: ''Several dependencies (clap_complete, comfy-table,
    csv, dirs, reqwest, toml) are declared directly in the crate instead of in [workspace.dependencies]
    as the story guardrails specify.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #6: ''RawConfig lacks #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].
    A typo like sever_url instead of server_url in cli.toml will be silently ignored,
    and the default http://localhost:8080 will be used instead.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer caught vacuous assertions in cli_structure.rs (is_err || is_ok
    tautologies) but did not flag the specific config test with assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) which is a different vacuous pattern. The config test vacuous assertion
    was missed.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion config test using 'let _ = config;'.
    Reviewer's vacuous test findings were limited to cli_structure.rs command group
    tests, not the config default test.
